  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1246 PM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nLatest model data continues to support a cooling and wetting trend\nacross all of south central and southeast Colorado through the end \nof week and into the weekend, as the upper high slides into \nSouthern High Plains, as an upper trough develops across the West \nCoast. This set up is a classic monsoonal pattern for Colorado, \nwith abundant moisture embedded within modest southwest flow aloft \nthrough the weekend. The available moisture, combined with upslope \nflow across the plains behind a passing front across the plains on \nThursday, will bring temperatures back down to at and even slightly \nbelow seasonal levels through the weekend, with expected daily rounds \nof showers and thunderstorms. We will likely need to issue flash flood\nwatches for area burn scars for Thursday, and additional flood products \nfor burn scars and other areas into the weekend, depending on coverage\nof heavy rain and how saturated soils may become. Those living in and \nnear the recent burn areas should remain weather through the weekend.    \n\nInto early next week, models support the upper high building back\nacross the Southern Rockies, leading to slight warming within more \nwesterly flow across the region. However, models continue to support\nample moisture within the westerly flow, for continued good coverage\nof daily showers and storms areawide into early next week.",
